# Sharing and live editing

There are two ways to work with other people: send a **file**, or work together on a **live link**.


::divider{aqua}
## Send a file

Every app can save its work as a file (see [Files](#/files)). Email it, put it in a drawer in Cabinet, or drop it anywhere. The other person opens it in the same app!

## Share & Chat

Apps with a **Share** tab (Cabinet, Mainkey, Formly, Hexa, Taskra, Delta and others) have a **Share & Chat** button. It starts a live session. Everyone who opens the link sees changes as they happen, and a chat panel lets you talk while you work. No account is needed!

## Overshare

[Overshare](https://overshare.radii-office.com) is a hosted place to share documents. Sign up, link a Writeout, Taskra or other Radii document, and everyone with the link edits it live. It also has **Groups**, like a team site, and keeps a history of changes. Overshare has three themes, New, Nova and Classic!

## Messaging

* **Phosphor** is a server-based chat app with servers, channels, roles, direct messages, voice and custom emojis!
* **Antimony** is a message board with spaces, posts and replies!
* **Beta** is a microblog, and **Mintcode** hosts code. See [Community apps](#/community)!

## What other people can do

| You share | They can |
| --- | --- |
| A file | Open and edit their own copy |
| A Share & Chat link | See and edit live while the session is open |
| An Overshare edit link | Edit live (you can limit this in Link Settings) |
| An Overshare view link | Read only |

::note Keep editing links private
Anyone who has an edit link can change the document. Treat it like a password, and use a view link when people only need to read!
::end
